IMPORT prelude

-- Public Utilities Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the water-supply offences an ordinary owner, contractor or plumber meets: the penalty for
-- each offence in Part 5 and the general penalty (s 58), the due-diligence defence and who loses it (ss 47, 47A, 50, 56A), storage
-- tank security (s 45A), who may do plumbing and design work (ss 40G, 40H and the definitions in s 2), the duty to enquire before
-- excavating (s 57), 5% controller notices (ss 44E, 44J), composition (s 59), recovery of unpaid bills (s 25) and refund claims (s 68B).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PUA2001.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 8 of 2026 (in force 29 May 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a member of the public,
-- a building owner, a contractor or a plumber meets. Not encoded: the Board's constitution, finances and Coastal and Flood Protection
-- Fund (Parts 2 and the Schedules), tariffs and the water conservation tax (ss 20, 20A), the Board's powers of entry and works, Part 3A
-- compensation and owner-initiated acquisition, plumber licensing procedure (ss 40I-40N), the duties in ss 40O-40Q, approved suppliers'
-- conditions (ss 42-44), the 12%/30%/indirect controller approvals and special administration (ss 44F-44M), and Parts 6 and 7 beyond
-- s 68B. Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit; the arrangement at its head is out of step with it from s 24 onwards.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Utilities Act 2001 -- water offences`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 39 entering Board premises without written consent`
    `s 40G(1)-(4) unlicensed regulated works`
    `s 40G(5)-(6) or 40H engaging the wrong person`
    `s 41 supplying drinking water without approval`
    `s 45 failing to maintain a water service installation`
    `s 45A storage tank security`
    `s 46 failing to mark or separate pipes`
    `s 47 damaging Board property`
    `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm`
    `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more`
    `s 47A(2) damaging a water installation and interfering with supply`
    `s 49 pretending to be a Board employee`
    `s 50(1) unauthorised connection, waste, contamination or disruption`
    `s 50(2)(a) dishonestly abstracting water`
    `s 50(2)(b) reselling Board water without consent`
    `s 50(2)(c) interfering with a meter`
    `s 50(2)(d) tampering with a meter`
    `s 51 obstructing the Board`
    `s 52 false statement`
    `s 57 excavating without enquiry`

§§ `Penalties -- each offence, and s 58 for the rest`

-- s 58: "Any person guilty of an offence under this Act for which no penalty is expressly provided shall be liable on conviction to a
-- fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence,
-- to a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day".
-- Express penalties: s 40G(7) $10,000 / 3 years; s 41(2) $50,000 / 5 YEARS; s 45A(5) $50,000 / 12 months, $1,000 a day; s 47(1)
-- $10,000 / 3 years; s 47A(1)(a) $40,000 / 3 MONTHS, but (b) "if the water main or connecting pipe is 300 mm or more in diameter"
-- $200,000 / 3 years; s 47A(2) $200,000 / 3 years; s 50(1) $50,000 / 3 years, $1,000 a day; s 50(2) $50,000 / 3 years, $2,500 a day;
-- s 57(1) $50,000 / 3 years. Sections 39, 40G(8), 40H, 45, 46, 49, 51 and 52 create offences with no penalty of their own.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general penalty applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 39 entering Board premises without written consent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 40G(5)-(6) or 40H engaging the wrong person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 45 failing to maintain a water service installation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 46 failing to mark or separate pipes` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 pretending to be a Board employee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 51 obstructing the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 52 false statement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the general penalty applies` `the offence` THEN 10000
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `s 40G(1)-(4) unlicensed regulated works` THEN 10000
        WHEN `s 47 damaging Board property` THEN 10000
        WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm` THEN 40000
        WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more` THEN 200000
        WHEN `s 47A(2) damaging a water installation and interfering with supply` THEN 200000
        OTHERWISE 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the general penalty applies` `the offence` THEN 12
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `s 41 supplying drinking water without approval` THEN 60
        WHEN `s 45A storage tank security` THEN 12
        WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm` THEN 3
        OTHERWISE 36

-- The further fine "for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction". Zero where the provision
-- gives none.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    IF `the general penalty applies` `the offence` THEN 250
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `s 45A storage tank security` THEN 1000
        WHEN `s 50(1) unauthorised connection, waste, contamination or disruption` THEN 1000
        WHEN `s 50(2)(a) dishonestly abstracting water` THEN 2500
        WHEN `s 50(2)(b) reselling Board water without consent` THEN 2500
        WHEN `s 50(2)(c) interfering with a meter` THEN 2500
        WHEN `s 50(2)(d) tampering with a meter` THEN 2500
        OTHERWISE 0

-- s 47A(1): the tier turns on the diameter alone -- "300 mm or more".
GIVEN `diameter in mm` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for damaging a water main` MEANS
    IF `diameter in mm` AT LEAST 300 THEN 200000 ELSE 40000

§§ `47, 47A, 50, 56A -- the due-diligence defence`

-- s 47(2), s 47A(3): "it is a defence ... to prove that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to
-- avoid the commission of the offence, but this defence is not available to any person who may be liable by virtue of section 56A".
-- s 50(6): the same defence "In any proceedings for an offence under subsection (1) or (2)(b) or (d)" -- "(but not by virtue of
-- section 56A)". So dishonest abstraction (s 50(2)(a)) and meter interference (s 50(2)(c)) have no such defence.
-- Damage under ss 47 and 47A is an offence "whether wilfully or otherwise".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence carries a due-diligence defence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 47 damaging Board property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main under 300 mm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 47A(1) damaging a water main of 300 mm or more` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 47A(2) damaging a water installation and interfering with supply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 50(1) unauthorised connection, waste, contamination or disruption` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 50(2)(b) reselling Board water without consent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 50(2)(d) tampering with a meter` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `liable only as employer or principal under s 56A` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the due-diligence defence succeeds` IF
        `the offence carries a due-diligence defence` `the offence`
    AND (NOT `liable only as employer or principal under s 56A`)
    AND `proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence`

-- s 56A: where an agent or employee commits an offence, the principal "shall ... be liable for that offence ... unless that other
-- person proves to the satisfaction of the court that the offence was committed without the consent or connivance, and that it was
-- not attributable to any neglect on the part, of that other person". Both limbs must be proved.
GIVEN `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is liable for the employee's offence` IF
    NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved no neglect`)

§§ `45A -- storage tank security`

-- s 45A(1): the duty applies to "a water service installation having a storage tank from which piped water suitable for drinking
-- (excluding NEWater) is drawn". (2) sets the detailed duties (authorised access only, kept locked, regular checks, records, notifying
-- the Board). (3): "Subsection (2) does not apply ... [to] any storage tank in residential premises which do not take their water
-- supply through a master meter." The general duty in (1) still applies to them.
GIVEN `drinking water is drawn from it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it holds NEWater` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45A covers the storage tank` IF
    `drinking water is drawn from it` AND (NOT `it holds NEWater`)

GIVEN `drinking water is drawn from it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it holds NEWater` IS A BOOLEAN, `residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `supplied through a master meter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detailed s 45A(2) duties apply` IF
        `s 45A covers the storage tank` `drinking water is drawn from it` `it holds NEWater`
    AND ((NOT `residential premises`) OR `supplied through a master meter`)

§§ `40G, 40H and s 2 -- who may do plumbing and design work`

-- s 2: "limited WSI design works" means designing a water service installation downstream of a meter "where the water service
-- installation being designed does not include any pumping equipment or storage tank". "regulated works" means sanitary works, limited
-- WSI design works or WSI works (not other WSI design works).
GIVEN `includes pumping equipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `includes a storage tank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the design works are limited WSI design works` IF
    (NOT `includes pumping equipment`) AND (NOT `includes a storage tank`)

DECLARE Work IS ONE OF
    `sanitary works`
    `WSI works`
    `limited WSI design works`
    `other WSI design works`

DECLARE Engagee IS ONE OF
    `a licensed plumber`
    `a worker directly supervised by a licensed plumber`
    `a professional engineer who is not a licensed plumber`
    `an unlicensed handyman`

-- s 40G(1): an individual must not carry out regulated works unless a licensed plumber or "under the direct supervision of a licensed
-- plumber". (9): (1)-(4) do not apply "to a professional engineer in respect of any limited WSI design works".
GIVEN `the person` IS AN Engagee, `the work` IS A Work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may carry out the work` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`
    WHEN `other WSI design works` THEN
        CONSIDER `the person`
        WHEN `a professional engineer who is not a licensed plumber` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the person`
        WHEN `a licensed plumber` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a worker directly supervised by a licensed plumber` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a professional engineer who is not a licensed plumber` THEN `the work` EQUALS `limited WSI design works`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 40G(5): an owner or occupier wanting sanitary works or WSI works "must only engage a person permitted under subsection (1) or (3)".
-- (6): for limited WSI design works, such a person "or (b) a professional engineer". s 40H(1): for WSI design works that are NOT
-- limited, "only engage a professional engineer". The owner's duty and the worker's permission coincide.
GIVEN `the person` IS AN Engagee, `the work` IS A Work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may engage the person` IF
    `the person may carry out the work` `the person` `the work`

§§ `57 -- duty to enquire before excavation`

-- s 57(1): digging "with any mechanical equipment, tool or explosive" without FIRST (a) obtaining the Board's plans or records, (b)
-- "carrying out trial trenches to physically ascertain the location" of mains, AND (c) complying with any Board requirements. All three
-- are required: missing any one is the offence ($50,000 or 3 years).
GIVEN `breaks ground with equipment, tool or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained the Board's plans` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dug trial trenches` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied with the Board's requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the excavation is an offence` IF
        `breaks ground with equipment, tool or explosive`
    AND NOT (`obtained the Board's plans` AND `dug trial trenches` AND `complied with the Board's requirements`)

§§ `44E, 44J -- notice by a 5% controller of a designated entity`

-- s 2 (Part 4A): a "5% controller" holds or controls "5% or more, but less than 12%". s 44E(1): notice to the Board "within 7 days after
-- becoming the 5% controller". Defences: (3) not aware, and notified "within a period of 14 days after becoming aware"; (4) the increase
-- came from an associate's holding, with no agreement or arrangement with that associate, and notice "within a period of 7 days after
-- the contravention". (5) otherwise lack of intent is no defence.
GIVEN `percentage held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 5% controller` IF
    `percentage held` AT LEAST 5 AND `percentage held` LESS THAN 12

GIVEN `days to notify after becoming a 5% controller` IS A NUMBER,
      `was unaware` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify after becoming aware` IS A NUMBER,
      `the increase came from an associate with no arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify after the contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to notify is an offence` IF
        `days to notify after becoming a 5% controller` GREATER THAN 7
    AND (NOT (`was unaware` AND `days to notify after becoming aware` AT MOST 14))
    AND (NOT (`the increase came from an associate with no arrangement` AND `days to notify after the contravention` AT MOST 7))

-- s 44J: (a) an individual -- $500,000 or 3 years, and $50,000 a day continuing; (b) "in any other case" -- $1 million, $100,000 a day.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum Part 4A Division 2 fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 500000 ELSE 1000000

§§ `59 -- composition`

-- s 59(1): the Board may compound "(a) any offence under section 45A ... a sum not exceeding $10,000; and (b) any other offence under
-- this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence ... not exceeding $3,000" (amended by Act 38 of 2024). Zero here means the
-- offence cannot be compounded.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `s 45A storage tank security` THEN 10000
    ELSE
        IF `prescribed as compoundable` THEN 3000 ELSE 0

§§ `25 -- recovering unpaid water bills`

-- s 25(1): an unpaid sum may be demanded by notice, with a prescribed fee, payable "within 7 days from the date of the notice". (2):
-- "If the amount and fee are not paid within the period of 7 days, a warrant may be issued" for seizure and sale of movable property.
-- (6): seized property may be sold by public auction "at any time after the end of 7 days from the date of the seizure, unless in the
-- meantime the amount of the debt and the costs ... have been paid". (8): a surplus unclaimed for 12 months goes to the Board's fund.
GIVEN `days since the notice` IS A NUMBER, `paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a distress warrant may issue` IF
    `days since the notice` GREATER THAN 7 AND (NOT `paid`)

GIVEN `days since the seizure` IS A NUMBER, `paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized property may be auctioned` IF
    `days since the seizure` GREATER THAN 7 AND (NOT `paid`)

GIVEN `months since the sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may still claim the surplus` IF
    `months since the sale` LESS THAN 12

§§ `68B -- refunds of overpaid fees, charges and taxes`

-- s 68B(1): "a person is not entitled to a refund ... Except as provided in this section". (3): only if "(a) the person makes the claim
-- within 5 years starting on the date of the overpayment ...; (b) the claim is in the form and manner required by the Board; and (c)
-- the Board is satisfied that there was an overpayment". Five years is taken here as 60 whole months.
GIVEN `months since the overpayment` IS A NUMBER, `claim in the Board's form` IS A BOOLEAN, `Board satisfied of the overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a refund may be made` IF
        `months since the overpayment` LESS THAN 60
    AND `claim in the Board's form`
    AND `Board satisfied of the overpayment`
